Provenance and licensing

This repository is a DSH plugin built on top of
https://github.com/ZhangYangyi03/autoforge (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Yangyi
Zhang). `service/autoforge_svc/` is a copy of that project rather than a fork
-- the same MIT terms and the same copyright holder apply to the copied
modules, which is why LICENSE carries the upstream copyright line unchanged.

The licence file is deliberately left as plain MIT text. An earlier version of
it appended a scope note; GitHub then reported the repository licence as
`NOASSERTION` instead of `MIT`, because the licence detector reads the file it
is given and a file with extra prose stops being the licence it started as.
The note lives here instead, where it belongs: it is provenance, not terms.

What this repository adds or changes, all under the same MIT terms:

  - `lib/index.js` -- the DSH side: tool mounting, the per-turn brief, the
    schema projection that keeps 73 tool schemas out of every request in full.
  - `presets/autoforge.patch.yml` and the other files in `presets/`.
  - `service/autoforge_svc/service.py` -- the stdio service that exposes the
    copied modules over a line protocol (76 methods).
  - `service/autoforge_svc/tests/` and `service/autoforge_svc/tests/regression/`
    -- the unit tests and the assertion suites.
  - the modules listed under "有改动的模块" in README.md.

